The battery's average (device/main_fm1.c): batt_raw + (b - batt_raw) / 16 never moved for a difference under 16 (the
division rounds it to 0), so the reading stayed near its first value until the next power-on, and the bars with it.
The average is kept x16 now (batt_q4, device/plat_fm1.c), so a small change adds up. Both branches (FM1_BATT_EVERY,
the key scan's reading, or the main loop's own) share the line.
The host simulator: "battery RAW" sets what plat_battery_raw gives (upstream's fixed 620 at the start).
plat_battery_raw itself is upstream's now (f54cba3, APP_BATTERY_RAW in app.h).
Why MIDIMON needs it: a battery percentage (GLO 1/3) that follows the battery, not only the stock firmware's bars.
Applies to: fm1-base 317cb86, after 0001-0002. Upstream: not offered yet.
diff --git a/device/main_fm1.c b/device/main_fm1.c
index b0e181c..5aa8f83 100644
--- a/device/main_fm1.c
+++ b/device/main_fm1.c
@@ -1373,8 +1373,11 @@ static void fm1_main(void)
             int32_t b = fm1_adc_read(FM1_ADC_BATT);
 #endif
             batt_t = fm1_ms;
-            if (b > 0)
-                batt_raw = batt_raw ? batt_raw + (b - batt_raw) / 16 : b;
+            if (b > 0) {                            /* a sixteenth of the way each time, kept x16: the plain
+                                                     * (b - batt_raw) / 16 never moved for a difference under 16 */
+                batt_q4 = batt_q4 ? batt_q4 + b - (batt_q4 + 8) / 16 : b * 16;
+                batt_raw = (batt_q4 + 8) / 16;
+            }
         }
         fm1b_dbg.stage = 2;                         /* (breadcrumbs: where a watchdog reset found the loop) */
         ble_poll();                                 /* Bluetooth's tasks, once started */
